{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Sarah denied, saying, 'I did not laugh.</b>' Our mother Sarah, who was a righteous woman — how is it possible that she did not believe the words of the angel, and was she not a prophetess? And our Rabbis of blessed memory said: Abraham was subordinate to Sarah in prophecy, as it says (Genesis 21:12): ״כל אשר תאמר אליך שרה שמע בקולה״ — 'in all that Sarah says to you, listen to her voice'; and surely there is no prophet who does not know that angels are the emissaries of the Holy One, blessed be He, and all their words are from the mouth of HaShem. And furthermore, not only did she not believe, but she denied it after the angel said to him, 'Why did Sarah laugh?' And the answer to this is that our father Abraham knew that they were men, and recognized through his wisdom that they were angels, as I have hinted — but this recognition and knowledge was not in Sarah, and she supposed that they were men like other men, and did not believe their words, and therefore laughed. And as for her denying that she had not laughed — she did so out of fear of Abraham, for she thought that Abraham was saying this from recognizing her face, and when he persisted in his word, saying ״לא כי צחקת״ — 'No, for you did laugh' — then it became clear to her that he knew this from HaShem through prophecy, and she fell silent. Thus Ramban explained."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:20.639669469Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}